# RISC-V vector extension 1.0 and the ratified vector crypto and BF16 extensions
# (Zvbb, Zvbc, Zvkg, Zvkned, Zvknha/Zvknhb, Zvksed, Zvksh, Zvfbfmin, Zvfbfwma).
#
# Generated from riscv-opcodes (extensions/rv_v and rv_zv*) for the encodings and
# from LLVM's RISC-V disassembler (llvm-objdump -M no-aliases) for the mnemonic,
# including the segment forms vlseg<n>e<eew>.v etc., and the operand order.
# Every instruction lifts to a user operation named after it (dots become
# underscores) whose output is the written register (vd, rd or the FP rd) and
# whose inputs are its source operands; the masked form (vm=0, ",v0.t") also
# takes the old vd and v0, and accumulating, slide-up and vector-crypto forms
# take the old vd. The element-wise semantics depend on vl and vtype at run time,
# which the user operations leave implicit, but the data flow between vector
# registers, scalar registers and memory addresses is kept.

